{
 "$schema_note": "Parity task suite. Each task is a deterministic script of MCP tool calls against a disposable fixture plus an oracle check defined BEFORE execution. Step forms: {call, args, [expect_error]} | {expect:{path, equals|gte|contains|not_equals}} | {sleep} | {key} (shorthand for call key). Coordinate sugar: target {client:[x,y]} = fixture client-relative point converted to a coordinate target in the latest full-screen raster; {client_zoom:[x,y]} = point inside the latest zoom raster; region {client:[x,y,w,h]} for zoom. {window:'second'} on a client target aims at the fixture's second window instead of the main one. Every task is repeated `repeats` times from a fresh fixture. Steps that need accessibility are marked optional_a11y and count as 'untested' (not failed) when get_app_state cannot see the app. macOS variant: fixtures are Chrome (served over the runner's loopback origin so the oracle needs no extra TCC grant) and a native AppKit app. Input is process-bound, so the runner prepends open_application(pid, activate:false) to every task with a fixture; that prelude is recorded separately from the task's own tool calls. A task the platform cannot express carries `skip` with the reason and is reported as skipped, not omitted.",
 "repeats": 5,
 "fixtures": {
  "browser": {
   "kind": "chrome-app",
   "file": "fixtures/browser.html",
   "size": [
    1000,
    800
   ],
   "position": [
    0,
    60
   ],
   "title_prefix": "CU-FIXTURE "
  },
  "native": {
   "kind": "appkit",
   "file": "fixtures/native-macos.m",
   "size": [
    800,
    600
   ],
   "title_prefix": "CU-NATIVE",
   "second_window_title": "CU-NATIVE-2",
   "note": "Purpose-built AppKit app with the same client-relative geometry as fixtures/native.py. Tk is not usable here: Tk/Aqua does not consume CGEvents posted to its process, so it could not distinguish a product failure from a toolkit one."
  }
 },
